{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/253106-apocalypse-vault","id":253106,"title":"Apocalypse Vault","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-09T00:28:11-07:00","id":253106,"title":"Apocalypse Vault","content":"Okay I feel the existence of the apocalypse vault is just begging for people to collect <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">apocalypses, so folks come share your end of the world ideas.<br /> <br /> The old stand bys are fine but please include the twist to make it different.<br /> <br /> Like say the meteor that hits earth is the last piece of a dead planet and now the literal ghost planet is spreading its power, or the local equivalent of Umbrella Co was studying the zombie virus and the werewolf disease and managed to accidentally make zombies who heal through essence expenditure and eat people to regain essence, that sort of thing.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:56:37-07:00","id":253322,"title":"","content":"The Wild Things are coming, the Wild Things are coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T12:27:57-07:00","id":253541,"title":"","content":"Where are those Apocalypse Vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-09-2014, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:16:43-07:00","id":253581,"title":"","content":"Setting wise, it's in the Seattle 1999 splinter. Bookwise, it's in Splintered City: Seattle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:33:10-07:00","id":253660,"title":"","content":"I could do worse than the Apocalypse World games I've been in. So:<ul><li>An airborne fungus that infects people's brains causing them to sleep walk and ultimately climb to a high vantage point before dying and releasing more spores.</li> <li>A psychic darkness that cloaks the entire world, driving those who stray from the light mad or turns them against their fellow humans.</li> </ul>Or some of the (averted) end game scenarios from my Wod games:<ul><li>Plague of Abyssal Brain Spiders who at the end of their life cycle consume the brain and become Azlu</li> <li>The Second Great Chicago Fire</li> <li>Megavolcano in Northwest Territories</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/463-derendel","name":"Derendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T01:36:32-07:00","id":253918,"title":"","content":"I've thought that an azlu eating someone with brain spiders would lead to nothing good myself....<br /> <br /> Oh anyway, another idea I thought might be interesting a zoonotic virus pandemic: a virus that turns humans closer to their favored animal hosts, so picture how bad it would be if a pandemic that killed most but left the survivors brain fried beastmen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T10:08:27-07:00","id":254168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derendel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/253106-apocalypse-vault?p=253660#post253660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plague of Abyssal Brain Spiders who at the end of their life cycle consume the brain and become Azlu...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that sounds like the plot of David Wong's <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/This_Book_Is_Full_of_Spiders\" target=\"_blank\">This Book Is Full of Spiders, Seriously Dude Don't Touch It!</a></i>, which I mean in a GOOD way!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T20:08:43-07:00","id":254980,"title":"","content":"A few obvious ones that seem ripe for crossover to me. And an artifact. (another might be written up)<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------<br /> 1: Fall of the Old Kingdom.<br /> <br /> In the Ancient past the Sin-Eaters and Deathlords reigned over what was a major empire of the dead. They once wielded nearly unfettered control over death in their cults. Over time pride, envy, and politics brought it into conflict with itself. Eventually it turned into a civil war with the various factions bringing forward enough power to shake the realms of the dead. When the God-Machine sealed this apocalypse, the involved Deathlords fell into slumber and their cults collapsed. <br /> <br /> Should this apocalypse be released, the powers that were unleashed would cause the gateways of the world that lead into The Autochthonous Depths to spew forth its inhabitants. As the remaining Deathlords stir they cause parts of their ruined kingdoms to begin to overlay onto the living world. With the shattered realm appearing the lives of everyone near them are thrown into chaos... along with the infrastructure of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------<br /> 2: The Father's Grave<br /> <br /> The great forefather of the Werewolves prowled the world in a previous eon separating the worlds of flesh and spirit. When the Firstborn struck down the Father Wolf they disrupted the Gauntlet that seprates the Shadow and the physical realm was briefly bridged. Many of the ancient spirits that had managed to avoid Father Wolf's path took the opportunity to try and spread into the physical realm. Compounding that, the site of Father Wolf's grave became the site of the first Wound(a place spiritually poisoned) and fount of power for the Maeljin, powerful spirits who reflect madness, suffering, hate, trechery and self destruction. When the God-Machine sealed this apocalypse, after Father Wolf's death but before the consequences could be truely felt. The Gauntlet was restored, the invading spirits were cast out and the actual site disappeared. <br /> <br /> Should this apocalypse be released, the power of the gauntlet would weaken terribly. Hoards of Spirit-Urged, Claimed, and Ridden would appear all over the world. The Maeljin would also be bolstered by the return of what is perhaps one of the largest Wounds in history. The Pure tribes may desire for this to come to pass, not realizing that the Maeljin would come even as the Gauntlet fell though the Bale Hounds would no matter what. The chaos ahd suffering from the emergence of the Spirits would strengthen the Maeljin even without the return of the Wound. With all of the disruptions it would cause the GOd-Machine would lose a good portion of its Human resources and yet would need to expend even more energy defending against the Ridden and Maeljin.<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Artifact: The Assembly<br /> <br /> Back in the early 20th century there was a group of Europeans who got it into their head that they would be able to conquer and rule over the world. They were optimistic that they would succeed in their endevor and that Europe would belong to them by the 1950's. They were a tad, shall we say, elitist and that Europe would be quickly purged of all inferior individuals through various methods. Their new Utopia could only then take form, but they quickly decided that the previous forms of their citizens would not be suited for living in it. Fortunately, they knew a mage and what that mage was capable of. The mage tasked with creating the new Humanity. When they met again the mage revealed the cube.<br /> <br /> &quot;The cube is a rather simple in its use but dramatic in effect. Once placed on a surface outside of its confinement it will then procede to melt and absorb all surrounding materials including people, structures and books. It is designed such that all of in information that is absorbed, such as the written word or human memories, would be stored in the expanding mass. It will continue to grow until it covers an area roughly the size of mainland Europe. The Mass then would contain not only all of the knowledge of Europe but also the mental will of its inhabitants. This strength would allow the mass to modify its shape as it needs, it could easly move under its own power and repair any damage that other nations could do to it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the group then had a moment of lucidity and buried the research and the mage. It went forgotten until a servant of the God-Machine discovered it and it was moved to the vault.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This artifact is extremely dangerous to handle except by moving it in its container. It is essentally a Doomsday device. Actually using it as intended would create a mass from a lot of terrified and angry people. Consider then what damage it could unleash if one of the people was a mage, or if a library of the arcane was in it. Also unless the activator had a great escape plan they would almost certanly be absorbed or its first target.<br /> <br /> Its true value does not actually lay in using the entire cube. Touching it while in cover would be almost certanly fatal (roll resist damage, cover is destroyed and the user is forced to enter demonic form. Essentially going loud). Manipulating it while in demonic form is possible and it will do 1 aggrivated damage each turn while being touched in that form. Succeeding in a extended strength roll will allow the demon to get a single grain submass of the cube. <br /> This grain is extremely versitile in the right hands. Assuming you can find a way to store it, after charging the grain with 1 Aether, any individual or object to come into contact will be absorbed by the grain submass. At this point the possible actions are only limited by time and imagination.<br /> <br /> For Example: using Animate on the submass will allow the Demon who charged the grain to command it and it will behave as a loyal form of the absorbed being and can be questioned freely. <br /> Some Demonic forms, such as but not limited to Amorphous or Dataform, can probe the mind of the Submass to gather information directly including embeds and exploits from creations of the God-Machine.<br /> This could also theoretically be used to defeat extremely powerful individuals in a single attack though angels in cover might sacrifice it to escape.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1428-sicol","name":"Sicol","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T09:36:19-07:00","id":255358,"title":"","content":"<b>The Most Beautiful of Heavens</b><br /> <br /> It would surprise any demon to find out that one of the twelve major apocalypses involved the God-Machine getting what it wanted, but that's what the deep green sphere is. It was a move that would allow the God-Machine to enact it's will perfectly, and turn the world into an absolute paradise.<br /> <br /> What's the catch? Two things.<br /> <br /> 1) The God-Machine is a jealous god. Within it's sight, others gods are an abomination. This most beautiful of heavens had to be shared, and that wasn't tolerable.<br /> 2) For whatever reason, the God-Machine needs humans. This heaven had all sorts of living things in it, but no humans, not anymore.<br /> <br /> Here's what happened. In the year 2007, the God-Machine invaded a plane of existence called the Hedge. It spent time probing it, exploring the thorns and paths, and setting up markers throughout much of the place.<br /> <br /> And then it observed Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Oh, it couldn't get in there. Not easily-the rules needed to do so were not the God-Machine's forte to follow, it needed a more human touch, and its' angels just weren't quite up to the task. It found demons could, but often they were kicked out or broken apart, if they could be made to try at all. But it still found out about the capabilities of the Fae, particularly within their Domains. It devised several theories about how they seemed to be one with their lands, and all the while devised a plan to exploit The Shining Domains.<br /> <br /> In August of 2008, it succeeded. Well. Sort of.<br /> <br /> In August of 2008, the God-Machine took advantage of the many markers placed in the Hedge, extrapolated details based on it's own infrastructure and jury rigged them for the purpose....and then executed a sustained version of Two Places At Onces.<br /> <br /> Reality was invaded by the Thorns. Arcadia was at everyone's door.<br /> <br /> The consequences were immeadiate. No longer bound to Ironside for a limited time, the Fae went nuts with it's new playground. The God-Machine responded in kind. It was war, and humanity had to pick their tyrants. A lot sided with the Machine if for no other reason than it represented what they knew. A great deal more didn't really have a choice, as far as the Fae were concerned.<br /> <br /> That war still goes on within that apocalypse, but that's not the worst of it. See, before the God-Machine could call things quit, the Strangers invaded Facilities, took over Control and Command Infrastructure, and through processes even they don't fully understand, <i>replaced them with themselves</i>. True Fae with all the mortal power of the God-Machine. Several facilities fell, one at a time.<br /> <br /> The G-M cut them off from the rest of itself and began shoring up defenses and enacting counter-offensives, but it observed that once they had done this, that could(and did) transplant their domains in Arcadia over huge swaths of Ironside the same way that the G-M did with the Hedge. In one desperate move to level the playing field, it left programs in every facility shortly after the first fell, and when enough did, it sent out the signal and did Two Places At Once again, using the True Fae as his markers this time.<br /> <br /> Well, it worked. Arcadia and Reality completely became one.<br /> <br /> Over time, things settled out. The Strangers preferred games to war, and while the God-machine was an worthy thing to play against, it also wasn't any fun-it didn't want to play game,s it wanted to enact Heaven.<br /> <br /> So within it's slice of the new world, it had done so. But it was bordered by heretic fate-powered machine-gods. All of humanity was pretty much Changed. Angels fell and became something else, out of context problems for both Fae and Machine.<br /> <br /> Was it worth continuing? Could the Machine defy the pagan gods?<br /> <br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> Reset.<br /> <br /> Record.<br /> <br /> Lock Away.<br /> <br /> <b>The Obligatory One</b><br /> <br /> THere are about....eight apocalypses, grouped together. It's hard to tell why the other four aren't inherently included with them. They aren't labeled, except to angels and demons.<br /> <br /> Those labels read Gehenna, Apocalypse, Ascension, Doomsday, Long Winter, Armageddon, Going Westward, and Twilight of the Gods.<br /> <br /> It takes some digging, but eventually one can find a note attached to each one, assumedly, if you can believe it, from the God-Machine itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;These were bad days.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T10:01:18-07:00","id":255372,"title":"","content":"Someone needs to convert the D-Reaper from Digimon Tamers into an apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T22:53:14-07:00","id":255853,"title":"","content":"You know it occurred to me that the apocalypse vault could be a way to make use of the translation guides what with the owod going out with a bang, or multiple bangs. <br /> <br /> Anyone familiar with Curse the Darkness? They have a supplement that includes a translation guide into the nwod system, so I've liked the idea of a Voice sending out shadows to eat anyone who breaks its rules of &quot;N<span style=\"color:#2C2C2C\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">o more ideology, religion, politics, or racism. The only rule is that everyone takes care of everyone or else.&quot; and how the various splats would react to it. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T09:56:24-07:00","id":256113,"title":"","content":"I actually did think of that, and I approve of every bit of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_l